  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_shutdown_executor_values",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_execute_API.c",
    "description": "During request shutdown, zend_shutdown_executor_values() unconditionally calls zend_hash_graceful_reverse_destroy(&EG(symbol_table)), which iterates buckets and invokes zend_unclean_zval_ptr_dtor/i_zval_ptr_dtor on each zval. In this PoV, a corrupted/invalid zval remains in EG(symbol_table), so refcount teardown reaches zend_gc_delref() with a wild pointer and crashes on read of p->refcount. The root cause is missing integrity validation/sanitization of symbol-table zvals before destructor-based teardown (unsafe propagation of invalid zval state into generic refcounted destructor path).",
    "conditions": "The fuzzed tracing-JIT request must produce malformed runtime state (via parser/JIT-executed script) such that EG(symbol_table) contains at least one entry whose zval type/GC pointer is invalid but still treated as refcounted at shutdown. On normal request shutdown (fast_shutdown=false), zend_hash_graceful_reverse_destroy triggers ht->pDestructor (zend_unclean_zval_ptr_dtor), which calls i_zval_ptr_dtor and eventually zend_gc_delref on the bogus pointer, causing the ASan SEGV."
  },
